---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import EvidenceBadge from '../components/EvidenceBadge.astro';
import Recollection from '../components/Recollection.astro';
import { withBase } from '../lib/paths';
---

<BaseLayout title="Units">
  <span class="eyebrow">The organization question</span>
  <h1>Units</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    What outfit was Larry actually in? His memory is specific — a designation, a size, a mix of
    trades — and that specificity is the best starting evidence the project has. But remembered
    terminology is not assumed to be exact, and no unit identification is treated as settled yet.
  </p>

  <h2>118th AOD — Aviation Operations Detachment <EvidenceBadge level="unverified-recollection" /></h2>
  <Recollection attribution="Larry's account, as related by his family">
    He remembers his organization as the 118th AOD — Aviation Operations Detachment. He describes
    the organization as relatively small, approximately 110 men, including radio operators and
    pathfinders. Some personnel reportedly required special clearances.
  </Recollection>
  <p>
    Research directions: the <strong>118th Aviation Company</strong> and units associated with it;
    the structure and naming of <strong>Aviation Operations Detachments</strong> in Vietnam during
    1964&ndash;1965; and where a detachment of radio operators and pathfinders of about that size
    would have fit in Army aviation's order of battle. Morning reports and unit histories are the
    most likely documents to settle the designation.
  </p>

  <h2>1st Cavalry association <EvidenceBadge level="unverified-recollection" /></h2>
  <p>
    Larry recalls being associated with the <strong>1st Cavalry</strong>. One open research
    question: the 1st Cavalry Division (Airmobile) arrived in Vietnam around September 1965, at
    the end of Larry's tour. The association he remembers may involve the division's advance
    elements, a different organization carrying the cavalry designation, or a connection formed at
    another point in his service. The memory is preserved as given while this is investigated.
  </p>

  <h2>What would settle it</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Larry's personnel records (DD-214 and service file)</li>
    <li>Morning reports for candidate units, 1964&ndash;1965</li>
    <li>Unit histories and operational reports of Army aviation organizations in-country</li>
    <li>Orders or photographs showing unit insignia or designations</li>
  </ul>

  <p>
    Progress is tracked on the <a href={withBase('/research/')}>research pages</a>.
  </p>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .lede {
    font-size: 1.15rem;
  }

  h2 :global(.evidence) {
    vertical-align: middle;
    margin-left: 0.5rem;
  }
</style>
